flsettings -- FreeLFS settings
==============================

Pages behind a sidebar: General (theme, panel labels), Display, Mouse &
touchpad, Keyboard (pages.c), Workspaces (workspaces.c), Date & time (datetime.c) and Wi-Fi, then Snapshots and About. `flsettings --page
general|display|mouse|keyboard|workspaces|datetime|wifi|snapshots|about` opens on that page; if Settings
is already running the page is passed to it (a socket in $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR) and
the new process exits.

General: settings are written to ~/.config/freelfs/desktop.conf ($FLUI_CONF
overrides the path):

	theme=dark|light
	panel_labels=0|1
	keyboard=de|us|uk|fr
	pointer_speed=-100..100  pointer_accel=adaptive|flat  left_handed=0|1
	mouse_natural=0|1  touchpad_natural=0|1  tap_click=0|1  typing_disable=0|1
	key_repeat_delay=ms  key_repeat_rate=per second  numlock=0|1
	night_light=0|1  night_warmth=0..100  brightness=percent
	mode=1920x1080@60  scale=100|125|150|200

The panel, flterm and flsettings pick changes up at once (inotify). A
keyboard choice is switched live through fl_shell (set_keyboard_layout) and
written to /etc/keyboard.conf (LAYOUT=de; $FL_KEYBOARD_CONF overrides) when
the user may write it; otherwise only keyboard= in desktop.conf is saved and
the window says so.

Display (display.c, screens on fldisplay): an arrangement of the outputs as rectangles (drag to move;
they snap edge to edge), and per output the resolution and refresh dropdown, scale 100-200 %, Enabled and
Primary. Apply runs `fldisplay set NAME mode=WxH@HZ scale=S pos=X,Y enabled=0|1 primary=1` for each changed
output, then a "Keep these settings?" bar counts down 15 s; Keep leaves it, otherwise `fldisplay revert`
runs (also when Settings closes during the countdown). `fldisplay list` gives one tab-separated line per
output: NAME, connected|disconnected, WxH@HZ or -, SCALE, X,Y, enabled|disabled, primary|-, MODES.
Night light: nightlight=off|on|auto, nightlight_temp 2700..6500 (the warmth slider), nightlight_from and
nightlight_to HH:MM; night_light=0|1 and night_warmth are written too, for flcomp's older keys.
Brightness is the backlight's sysfs file (FLSETTINGS_BACKLIGHT=DIR for tests); it needs write access: the
udev rule 90-flsettings-backlight.rules gives group seat that. Without a backlight the page says so.
Wallpaper is on this page too (`--page wallpaper` opens it).
Bluetooth (bluetooth.c): bluetoothctl only (show, power, devices, info, --timeout 10 scan on, pair, trust,
connect, disconnect, remove). Paired devices with connect/disconnect, Forget and the battery; nearby devices
after Search (10 s), Pair runs pair, trust and connect. No adapter: "No Bluetooth adapter found".
Printers (printers.c): CUPS tools only (lpstat -p -d, lpinfo --include-schemes dnssd,ipp,ipps,usb -v,
lpadmin -E -m everywhere / -x, lpoptions -d, lp, cancel -a). Set as default, test page, cancel jobs, remove
(asked first); without lpstat: "Printing is not installed". Every command is a helper sequence (cmd.c):
it runs with pipes read by the event loop, never blocking the window; a failure shows its stderr.
Mouse & touchpad: speed, acceleration profile, left-handed, natural scrolling for
mouse and touchpad separately, tap to click, disable while typing; flcomp applies
them through libinput. Keyboard: the four layouts (also written to
/etc/keyboard.conf when writable), repeat delay and rate, Num Lock at start, a
field to try it, and a read-only list of the keyboard shortcuts (flcomp's: Super, Alt-Tab,
Super+arrows, Print, ...; keep it in step with src/flcomp/seat.c and docs/M7-DESIGN.md).
Pages that do not fit the window scroll (wheel or bar).

Workspaces (workspaces.c): "Across" and "Down" steppers (1 to 8 each), the total with a small picture of the grid and
the quick choices 1, 2, 4, 6 and 8 (1x1, 2x1, 2x2, 3x2, 4x2). All of it is one key, workspaces=COLSxROWS in
desktop.conf (a bare N, written by hand, is N x 1; the default without the key is 2x2, flcomp's), written with
fl_conf_set like the other settings. flcomp applies it at once: windows on workspaces that are taken away move to the
last one that is left, and the panel's pager follows. The page says that, and lists Super+Ctrl+arrows (switch),
Super+Shift+arrows (move the window) and Super+Tab (overview); the Keyboard page's shortcut list has the same three.
The pager's right-click menu in flpanel writes the same key. `make check` runs tests/workspaces.py (headless flcomp,
clicks on the steppers and quick choices, desktop.conf and flcomp's announced grid checked; FLCOMP=, FLSETTINGS=,
SHMCLIENT=, APPS_OUT=DIR for screenshots, APPS_THEME=light APPS_SUFFIX=-light).

Wi-Fi: iwd's D-Bus API (net.connman.iwd on the system bus, libdbus;
$DBUS_SYSTEM_BUS_ADDRESS overrides the bus). Lists networks with signal bars
and a lock, scan, connect, disconnect, forget, the Wi-Fi switch, a Wired status
line. iwd asks for passwords through net.connman.iwd.Agent, exported by this
program; the typed password is wiped after it is sent and never logged. The
user needs access to iwd on the bus: group seat (iwd-seat.conf), wheel or
netdev. Without D-Bus, iwd, permission or hardware the page says so.

Build: make; make install (PREFIX, DESTDIR). Needs libflui, libdbus and
flcomp's protocol/fl-shell.xml (PROTO=...). Test without a compositor:
FLUI_PPM=out.ppm flsettings. Headless test with a stand-in iwd: tests/fakeiwd.c
and `apps.py flsettings` in src/flcomp/tests.

Date & time (datetime.c): a world map (libflui's fl_worldmap, Natural Earth projection)
with a dot for every place in tzdata's zone.tab. Click anywhere: the zone whose place is
nearest is chosen; a hover shows the nearest place with its local time and UTC offset,
and outlines its region (land nearer to that place than to any other). The chosen zone
has a pin and a card, its own region is tinted strongly and every region that shows the
same time right now softly. The search field above the map takes a city, country or zone
name ("berlin", "new york", "japan"), Up/Down and Enter or a click choose. Below: the
big local time, city, country, abbreviation, offset and zone name.
Choosing runs the helper fltime-set (src/fltime): /etc/localtime and /etc/timezone are
written, tz_changed= in desktop.conf is set so the panel redraws its clock at once (it
also calls tzset() each time). Clock: 24-hour or 12-hour (clock_24h=1|0 in desktop.conf,
used by the panel). Date and time: "Set time automatically" is the ntp service
(fltime-set ntp on|off; the line under it says when it last synchronised, from
/run/fltime.status; "Sync now" asks again). With it off, a date (YYYY-MM-DD) and time
(HH:MM) field and "Set" set the clock in the chosen zone (fltime-set time). When the
helper may not be run (the account is not in the group seat) or is missing, the page
says so in red and nothing changes.
Test hooks: FLTIME_SET, FLTIME_CONF, FLTIME_STATUS, FL_TZ_ETC, FL_ZONEINFO, FL_NOW (a fixed
time); for FLUI_PPM screenshots FLSETTINGS_TEST_MOUSE=x,y, FLSETTINGS_TEST_SEARCH=text,
FLSETTINGS_SIZE=WxH. tests/datetime.py drives the page in a headless flcomp.

Snapshots (snapshots.c): the btrfs snapshots flsnap keeps (src/flsnap): date, reason, package count; "Take a
snapshot", "Go back to this" (asks first; the current system is kept as a snapshot, restart to use it) and "Delete".
When the system runs from a snapshot a banner offers "Make this the current state". All of it runs /usr/bin/flsnap
(setuid root for group seat); $FLSNAP names another program for tests (the real flsnap with FLSNAP_MOCK=DIR).
`flsettings --page snapshots`.

Themes: General > Appearance has "More in Themes" (opens fltheme: fonts, window buttons, title bar, panel edge,
height and icons, animations, presets). Switching Dark/Light here also runs `fltheme --hints` so GTK's settings.ini follows.

Accent colour, wallpaper and sounds (2026-11, roadmap A4, A5, A7).
General > Appearance: six swatches (green, teal, blue, amber, orange, rose), written as accent= to
desktop.conf; libflui derives the theme from it (accent, text on it, selection fill) and every app
that watches the file, the panel and Settings itself included, redraws at once. flcomp reads the same
key for the volume indicator, the Alt-Tab frame and the lock screen. The crash screen keeps its own
green. General > Sounds: "System sounds" (sounds=0|1, default on) and a Test button (runs
`flsound --force notification`).
Display > Wallpaper (wallpaper.c): wallpaper=accent (default: the 3D F in the accent colour), a colour
name (one of the six built-in variants /usr/share/flcomp/wallpaper[-NAME].flw from flsplash's genart)
or user:NAME (an imported picture). "Match the accent colour" is the switch for the first. Import: type
or paste the path of a PNG or JPEG and "Use picture": it is decoded once (libpng, libjpeg; alpha is
mixed with the desktop colour, no CMYK, up to 64 megapixels), scaled down to fit 2560 x 1440 (never
enlarged) and saved as $XDG_DATA_HOME/freelfs/wallpapers/NAME.flw, the format flcomp loads
("FLWALL01", x, y, w, h, 3, size, deflate of the R, G, B planes, rows delta coded). flcomp watches
desktop.conf and swaps the wallpaper without a restart. "Remove" deletes an imported picture.
`flsettings --set-wallpaper FILE` does the import and sets it without a window (for the image viewer
and scripts). FLCOMP_SHARE moves the built-in directory (tests, screenshots).
